# Vulnerabilities in packages VENDORED INSIDE setuptools (setuptools/_vendor/).
#
# These cannot be fixed by bumping our own dependencies. Our direct pins are
# already clean: wheel 0.47.0 and setuptools 79.0.1 both scan with zero
# findings. What Trivy flags is the older copies setuptools bundles internally.
#
# The only way to replace them is to upgrade setuptools past 79.0.1, and that is
# pinned for a hard runtime reason documented in requirements.txt: setuptools
# 80.x removes the pkg_resources shim, Python 3.12 removed pkg_resources from
# the standard library, and fyers_apiv3's WebSocket client imports it. Upgrading
# breaks the market data feed outright.
#
# Reachability: these vendored modules are setuptools' own build-time machinery.
# The trading runtime never imports jaraco.context or wheel, and the exploit
# paths are archive extraction and package-index traversal, neither of which the
# bot performs. Re-evaluate whenever fyers_apiv3 stops depending on
# pkg_resources; at that point the setuptools pin can be lifted and this file
# deleted.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-08-08
CVE-2026-23949   # jaraco.context 5.3.0, vendored in setuptools
CVE-2026-24049   # wheel 0.45.1, vendored in setuptools
CVE-2025-47273   # setuptools 70.3.0, vendored copy
